From 350816dabb6a50fefe6e4a32c5606a9d1435ef4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 22:07:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] transports+configstore: tenant-scoped teams CRUD under
 /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/teams
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Starts extending the per-tenant admin surface beyond the inference
plane entities into governance metadata. Teams are tagging metadata
attached to VKs (and indirectly to customers) so the runtime registry
doesn't lazy-load them — the evictor pattern from providers / VKs /
MCP is intentionally not wired here. A team mutation shows up in
subsequent admin reads + on any VK whose team_id pointer the
operator updates.

configstore additions (delegate-then-verify, tenant_id re-pinned on
the row before delegating):
- ConfigStore.CreateTeamForTenant — pins tenant_id on the new row.
- ConfigStore.GetTeamsByTenant — list scoped to a tenant, with
  optional customer_id filter (same shape as GetTeams).
- ConfigStore.GetTeamByIDForTenant — single, cross-tenant ErrNotFound.
- ConfigStore.UpdateTeamForTenant — verify ownership, re-pin
  tenant_id, delegate to UpdateTeam.
- ConfigStore.DeleteTeamForTenant — verify ownership, delegate to
  DeleteTeam (which still handles the VK.team_id null-out + budget
  cascade).
- MockConfigStore stubs (single-implementation delegation).
- Tests cover: full create/list/get/update/delete happy path across
  two tenants showing isolation; cross-tenant GET/DELETE return
  ErrNotFound; malicious payload trying to migrate the team via
  tenant_id in body is re-pinned.

Transport additions:
- handlers.TenantTeamsHandler with POST/GET-list/GET-single/PUT/DELETE
  under /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/teams[/{team_id}]. POST mints
  a UUID when id is omitted. PUT accepts optional name + customer_id;
  empty patch → 400. DELETE returns 204 on success and 404 for
  cross-tenant probes.
- Wires into server.go under the same multi-tenant gate that mounts
  the provider/VK/MCP handlers.
- 8 handler tests covering: happy-path POST + minting; LIST tenant
  filter; GET cross-tenant 404; PUT happy path + empty body; DELETE
  happy path + cross-tenant 404 with target row preserved; nil-store
  rejection at construction.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
